 in the school without opening each case one by one. It helps the OSA or dean see problems early, like if violations are going up in one department.}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 \par }\pard \plain \ql \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs21 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \af0 {\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 \par }\pard \plain \ql \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs21 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \af0 {\b1 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 Figure 33. Record Violation Step 2: Select Violation}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 \par }\pard \plain \ql \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs21 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \af0 {\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 Figure 33 shows }{\b1 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 Step 2: Violation}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0  inside the Log a Violation process. The step indicator at the top shows that Step 1 (Student) is done and Step 2 (Violation) is now active. The heading says \uc1 \u8220 ?Select Violation\uc1 \u8221 ? with a search box that says \uc1 \u8220 ?Search violation code or title...\uc1 \u8221 ? The admin types here to find the right offense quickly. The list below shows every violation from the Rules & Regulations catalog. Each item displays the violation code and title (example: \uc1 \u8220 ?V-003 - Improper Uniform\uc1 \u8221 ?), a colored dot (yellow for Minor, orange for Major, red for Critical), and a severity badge on the right. The admin clicks the correct violation to highlight it with a red border, then clicks }{\b1 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 Next}{\fs24