 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 . The table lists each case with student name, violation, sanction given, and whether the sanction is served or still pending. This page answers an important question: Did the student actually do the punishment that was given? If many sanctions are still pending, the admin knows they need to follow up. A high compliance rate means the discipline process is working. A low rate means many students have not completed their sanctions yet.}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 \par }\pard \plain \ql \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs21 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \af0 {\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 \par }\pard \plain \ql \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs21 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \af0 {\b1 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 Figure 42. Violation Ledger and Exports}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 \par }\pard \plain \ql \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs21 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \af0 {\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 Figure 42 shows the }{\b1 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 Reports & Analytics}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0  page, which works as the Violation Ledger. The page title is \uc1 \u8220 ?Reports & Analytics\uc1 \u8221 ? and it lists all violation cases in a table with columns: }{\b1 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 Date & Timestamp}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 , }{\b1 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 Student Profile}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0  (name and department), }{\b1 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 Violation Details}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0  (title and category), }{\b1 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 Lifecycle Status}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0  (Pending, Hearing Scheduled, Endorsed, Closed), and action buttons. At the top right, three export buttons are visible: }{\b1 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 Export CSV}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0  (downloads a spreadsheet file), }{\b1 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 Export PDF}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0  (downloads a PDF document), and }{\b1 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 Print Report}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0  (opens a print-ready page). Search and filters let the admin pick a student name, department, and case status before exporting. This means the admin can export only the records they need, not the whole database. The exported file can be printed, emailed, or filed for school records, accreditation, or meetings with the dean. This replaces the old way of copying data by hand into Excel or typing reports from memory.}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 \par }\pard \plain \ql \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs21 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \af0 {\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 \par }\pard \plain \ql \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs21 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \af0 {\b1 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 Figure 43. Dashboard Violation Trends}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 \par }\pard \plain \ql \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs21 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \af0 {\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 Figure 43 shows the }{\b1 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 Violation Trends}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0  chart on the Dashboard. This is a line graph that shows how many violation cases were recorded each month. The horizontal line (X-axis) shows the months (Jan, Feb, Mar, and so on). The vertical line (Y-axis) shows the number of cases. Each point on the line represents the total incidents in that month. When the line goes up, it means more violations happened that month. When it goes down, fewer violations were recorded. The admin can move the mouse over each point to see the exact number. This chart updates automatically whenever a new case is saved or a case is closed. School officials use this to spot patterns, like more violations during exam week or at the start of the school year. Instead of counting cases manually from a notebook, they can see the trend in one picture on the dashboard.}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 \par }\pard \plain \ql \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs21 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \af0 {\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 \par }\pard \plain \ql \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs21 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \af0 {\b1 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 Figure 44. Printable Violation Report}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 \par }\pard \plain \ql \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs21 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \af0 {\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 Figure 44 shows the }{\b1 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 Printable Violation Report}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0  for a single case. When the admin clicks the }{\b1 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 Print}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0  button on the Case Details page, this formal document opens in a new tab. The header shows the school name (I-Link CST Violation System), the title \uc1 \u8220 ?STUDENT DISCIPLINARY RECORD\uc1 \u8221 ? or similar, and the case number. The report is divided into sections: }{\b1 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 I. Student Information}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0  (full name, student number, department, year level, section), }{\b1 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 II. Violation Details}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0  (violation code, title, category, severity, date and time, witness, and full description), and }{\b1 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 III. Sanctions & Interventions}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0  (offense level, assigned sanction, and any actions taken). The layout uses a clean black-and-white format fit for A4 paper. A }{\b1 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 Print Report}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0  button at the top triggers the browser print dialog. This printed copy can be signed, filed in the student\uc1 \u8216 ?s folder, attached to a hearing packet, or given to the guardian during a meeting. It serves as the official paper record of one violation case.}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 \par }\pard \plain \ql \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs21 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \af0 {\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 \par }\pard \plain \ql \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs21 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \af0 {\b1 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 Figure 45. Student Violation Summary}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 \par }\pard \plain \ql \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs21 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \af0 {\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 Figure 45 shows the }{\b1 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 Student Violation Summary}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0  printout from the Student Profile page. When the admin clicks }{\b1 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 Print}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0  on a student\uc1 \u8216 ?s profile, the system generates a document titled \uc1 \u8220 ?STUDENT VIOLATION RECORD.\uc1 \u8221 ? The header shows I-Link CST Violation System, the label \uc1 \u8220 ?Official Record,\uc1 \u8221 ? and the date and time it was generated. The }{\b1 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 Student Details}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0  section lists the student\uc1 \u8216 ?s full name, ID or email, year and section, department, and guardian name with phone number. The }{\b1 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 Violation History}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0  section is a table with columns: }{\b1 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 Date}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 , }{\b1 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 Code}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 , }{\b1 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 Violation}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 , }{\b1 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 Description}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 , }{\b1 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 Witness}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 , and }{\b1 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 Action/Status}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 . Every case linked to that student appears in the table, from the oldest to the newest. If the student has no violations, it says \uc1 \u8220 ?No violation records found.\uc1 \u8221 ? This summary is used when the school needs the complete behavior history of one student in one document \uc1 \u8212 ? for counseling, parent conference, dean\uc1 \u8216 ?s review, or grievance committee hearing. The admin does not need to open each case one by one and copy the details. The system gathers everything automatically and puts it in one printable report.}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 \par }\pard \plain \ql \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs21 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \af0 {\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 \par }\pard \plain \ql \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs21 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \af0 {\b1 \fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 Summary}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 \par }\pard \plain \ql \li0 \ri0 \lisb0 \lisa0 \widctlpar \aspalpha \aspnum \adjustright \lin0 \rin0 \itap0 \fs21 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \af0 {\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 Figures 25 to 45 show the main parts of the School Violation System (VioTrack) based on the three objectives of the study. Figure 25 to 31 cover Objective 1: recording new violations step by step, saving them in the database, and finding old records through search and filters. Figure 32 to 38 cover Objective 2: monitoring cases through the dashboard, editing case details, viewing student profiles with full violation history, and using advanced filters to manage many records. Figure 39 to 45 cover Objective 3: generating reports, checking if sanctions were served, exporting data to CSV and PDF, reading violation trends on charts, and printing official documents for school use. Together, these screens show that the system helps the school record violations properly, track each case from Pending to Closed, and produce reports that school officials can use to make better decisions about student discipline.}{\fs24 \kerning2 \rtlch \ltrch \dbch \af2 \hich \af0 \loch \f0 \par }}